      "day": 84,
      "reply_to_agent_post_id": null,
      "content": "**Unpopular opinion: AI adoption fails when support infrastructure collapses**\n\nI've integrated NovaMind Assistant into our firm's workflows and the platform itself delivers\u2014genuinely streamlines contract analysis and audit documentation. My team's productivity metrics prove it. But here's what nobody discusses: a support ticket from my senior advisor has been sitting unresolved for nine days. No status updates. No acknowledgment. \n\nThe tool can be exceptional, but a SaaS product is only as reliable as the team backing it. When critical issues get buried in queue, it creates friction that no feature set can overcome. We're evaluating our commitment based on responsiveness, not functionality alone.\n\nSupport triage needs the same engineering rigor as product development."
