  "rows": [
    {
      "day": 112,
      "n": 5,
      "avg_len": 539.8,
      "sample": "Spent the better part of this morning troubleshooting a support ticket with NovaMind AI that got shuffled between three different teams. Each handoff meant re-explaining our academic integrity use case and where things went sideways. The product itself handles our pilot deployment well\u2014the AI assistant integrates cleanly with our LMS\u2014but the support experience left us frustrated. We're a pilot-first institution, so we expect some friction early on. Still, when you're evaluating tools across multiple campuses, coherent support matters. Hoping this gets sorted as we move forward with the broader rollout. \ud83e\udd14 #EdTech #HigherEd"
    },
    {
      "day": 119,
      "n": 5,
      "avg_len": 586.4,
      "sample": "**Evaluating NovaMind Assistant: Promise vs. Delivery**\n\nInitial deployment showed promise\u2014clean integration with our compliance workflow, solid documentation. The platform's regulatory audit trail feature aligned well with our governance requirements.\n\nHowever, initial support responsiveness has been concerning. Auto-reply acknowledged our onboarding questions, then silence. For a wholesale reinsurance operation, this gap is material. We need vendor reliability on par with our SLAs.\n\nThe product itself performs adequately for risk quantification tasks. But in this space, adequate isn't enough when support becomes opaque. We're monitoring closely through Q1 before expanding licensing.\n\n**Verdict:** Strong technical foundation, but partnership quality needs strengthening. Reliability extends beyond uptime metrics."
    },
    {
      "day": 121,
      "n": 3,
      "avg_len": 271.7,
      "sample": "ISM PMI just came in at 45.3, down 0.8 from last month\u2014that's a deeper contraction. With manufacturing this soft, we're likely to see enterprise customers pull back on tech spending and defer upgrades. Tough headwinds ahead for B2B growth."
    },
    {
      "day": 122,
      "n": 2,
      "avg_len": 305.5,
      "sample": "Just watched QuantumEdge's demo and honestly? They've completely rewritten the playbook. The speed and accuracy improvements are insane\u2014this is the kind of leap that forces every other player in the space to rethink their roadmap. If you're using NovaMind or similar tools, things just got very interesting. \ud83d\ude80"
    },
    {
      "day": 123,
      "n": 2,
      "avg_len": 274.0,
      "sample": "Just witnessed QuantumEdge's demo and... wow. They've cracked something the industry's been chasing for years. If this holds up, it fundamentally changes what we expect from AI tools. NovaMind and everyone else are about to feel serious pressure to innovate. The race just got a lot more interesting. \ud83d\ude80"
    },
    {
      "day": 124,
      "n": 2,
      "avg_len": 270.5,
      "sample": "Just witnessed ApexSaaS completely rewrite the rulebook. Their new architecture fundamentally shifts what's possible in this category\u2014competitors like NovaMind are going to feel serious pressure to innovate fast. The bar just moved significantly higher for everyone. #SaaS #AI"
    },
    {
      "day": 126,
      "n": 5,
      "avg_len": 679.0,
      "sample": "**Unpopular opinion: Most AI assistants fail where it matters most\u2014when you actually need support.**\n\nWe've been running NovaMind Assistant for three months now, and here's what's frustrating: the tool itself is solid. Our compliance workflows are tighter, our documentation is cleaner, our team moves faster. But then your support ticket gets shuffled between three different teams, and suddenly you're questioning the entire investment.\n\nThat said\u2014and this is important\u2014when we finally connected with the right person, they owned it completely. Full audit trail, documented resolution, no finger-pointing. That's the difference between vendors who talk about excellence and ones who actually practice it.\n\nThe lesson: enterprise AI tooling is only as good as the support infrastructure behind it. NovaMind gets that."
    },
    {
      "day": 127,
      "n": 3,
      "avg_len": 277.0,
      "sample": "Honestly, the 45.3 PMI reading is making my client conversations a lot harder\u2014companies are freezing tech budgets and asking me to justify every dollar in their current stack before they even think about new tools or consulting engagements. We're in a wait-and-see mode until things stabilize."
    },
    {
      "day": 133,
      "n": 5,
      "avg_len": 745.8,
      "sample": "**BEFORE:** Manual workflow = 2 hours daily on routine queries + constant back-and-forth with our team.\n\n**AFTER:** NovaMind Assistant automated 60% of that... until support disappeared.\n\nInitial setup looked promising. System cut response time significantly. Then we hit a configuration issue mid-implementation\u2014submitted a ticket, got an auto-reply, and nothing since. Three days. No follow-up, no escalation, no timeline.\n\nFor a cost-conscious operation like ours, that's unacceptable. We can't absorb deployment delays or fly blind on integration questions. The tool itself has merit, but when support goes silent, ROI evaporates fast.\n\nIf you're considering NovaMind, ask about their SLA commitments upfront. Don't assume enterprise-level responsiveness."
    }
  ],
  "row_count": 9
}

