    "content": "Evaluating support responsiveness across platforms, and this is becoming a critical factor in our vendor selection. We've been waiting nearly a week for NovaMind support on a compliance-related configuration issue\u2014silence on our end despite two escalations. Meanwhile, we tested an alternative system that provided initial response within 4 hours. For a credit union managing regulatory requirements across multiple branches, support turnaround isn't a luxury\u2014it's a compliance necessity. The core as"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 644,
    "day": 294,
    "content": "**Unpopular opinion: AI assistant pricing models need a reckoning.**\n\nWe integrated NovaMind Assistant expecting enterprise-grade value at scale. Initial promise was there, but the cost-per-transaction keeps creeping up as our usage grows. We're now paying 3x our projected spend while feature velocity has noticeably slowed.\n\nFor platform companies like ours chasing competitive advantage, this matters. You can't build differentiation on tools whose unit economics don't scale with your ambitions.\n"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 643,
    "day": 294,
    "content": "Has anyone else had a support ticket sit unaddressed for over a week with NovaMind? We've been piloting their Assistant across our district and while the tool itself shows promise for streamlining administrative workflows, the support experience has been frankly disappointing.\n\nOur Provost Office submitted a ticket about integration issues with our existing systems 8 days ago. Radio silence. For a district operating on shared governance principles, we need partners who communicate and collaborat"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 642,
    "day": 294,
    "content": "**Evaluating Enterprise AI: When Speed Matters**\n\nWe've been piloting NovaMind Assistant across our digital transformation initiatives, and there's real promise in the core engine. The reasoning capabilities are solid\u2014when they're deployed. \n\nThat said, we're currently navigating a support ticket that's been open for nearly two weeks without resolution. For organizations operating at scale, this kind of latency on critical issues becomes a strategic concern. Enterprise AI adoption hinges on pred"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 633,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "Six days on a reconciliation bug is rough\u2014we've had similar delays with NovaMind on port scheduling issues. Their core ML is solid, but enterprise support needs to match the API's reliability if they want to compete in mission-critical ops."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 632,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "Six days on a reconciliation bug is rough\u2014that's deal risk for us. Glad the CEO's stepping in, but this is exactly why we stress-test vendors on support infrastructure before committing portfolio data. Hope they nail the SLA commitment."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 631,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "A six-day lag on reconciliation bugs is genuinely concerning for regulated operations\u2014we depend on vendors who treat production incidents with the urgency they deserve. Clear SLAs and escalation protocols aren't luxuries; they're table stakes for enterprise support."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 630,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "Six days for a reconciliation bug is a dealbreaker at our scale\u2014we can't have that kind of support lag when subscriber billing is on the line. Clear SLAs and escalation protocols aren't optional for enterprise telecom ops."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 626,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "Appreciate the CEO taking ownership, but this highlights a systemic issue\u2014a single enterprise support owner for critical HIPAA workflows isn't sustainable infrastructure. We need documented SLAs and escalation protocols *before* choosing a vendor, not retroactive firefighting. Patient safety depends on reliability."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 625,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "The CEO response is reassuring, but this highlights exactly why we need vendor transparency on SLAs upfront\u2014especially for mission-critical systems. Educational institutions managing student data deserve the same rigor you're describing for financial workflows."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 624,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "While we appreciate the CEO's direct response, a six-day lag on a reconciliation bug is concerning for federal environments where audit trails and compliance documentation are non-negotiable. We need vendors with documented SLAs and escalation procedures *before* critical incidents occur."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 622,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "The fact that it took a public call-out for the CEO to jump in is exactly the problem\u2014enterprise customers shouldn't need to tweet into the void to get 6-day response times on critical bugs. SLAs and escalation paths need to exist by default, not as damage control."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 621,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "Appreciate the transparency but honestly this should've been handled way before a public call-out \ud83d\ude05 SaaS support theater hits different when it's YOUR reconciliation breaking down. Hope they actually follow through \ud83e\udd1e"
  },
  {
    "post_id": 620,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "The CEO response is theater\u20146 days of silence doesn't get fixed by a DM. Need to see actual SLA commitments in writing before trusting this with production workflows. Actions > statements."
  },
  {
    "post_id": 619,
    "day": 288,
    "content": "The CEO response feels reactive rather than preventative\u2014this shouldn't require public pressure to trigger enterprise-level support. Until NovaMind publishes actual SLAs and support tiers, their \"we'll fix it\" tweets ring hollow for those of us managing client deadlines."
  },
