    {
      "post_id": 974,
      "day": 364,
      "content": "Filed a critical bug report with NovaMind Assistant three weeks ago\u2014asset lifecycle modeling functionality completely failed during our Q3 sustainability compliance review. Radio silence since then.\n\nSwitched to a manual audit process with our legacy system. Slower, yes. But at least we have visibility into the work and timely responses from support.\n\nFor a vendor handling safety-critical operations and regulatory requirements at this scale, communication gaps are unacceptable. We need partners who understand that in our industry, every day counts.\n\nHoping this gets escalated properly. Otherwise, we'll be reassessing our tooling strategy.\n\n#EnergyTech #SafetyCritical"
    },
    {
      "post_id": 975,
      "day": 364,
      "content": "Just spent 45 minutes on a support ticket that got passed between three different teams at NovaMind. Each handoff meant re-explaining the same UX blocker. That's three context resets on something that should've been routed correctly the first time. When your research tool creates friction *outside* the research process, it's hard to justify the subscription cost to stakeholders who are already questioning our tooling budget."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 976,
      "day": 364,
      "content": "Tested NovaMind Assistant against Anthropic's Claude for our CRM workflow integration last week. Claude handled the nuanced property transaction analysis with noticeably sharper contextual awareness\u2014especially on complex contingency language parsing.\n\nMore frustrating though: I've been waiting *four days* for NovaMind support to address a fundamental API integration issue. Complete radio silence. As someone who depends on reliable tooling for client deliverables, this level of response lag is disqualifying. The platform shows promise on output quality, but enterprise-grade support isn't optional when you're managing time-sensitive transactions.\n\nSwitching my team to Claude for now. Happy to revisit if support improves materially."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 977,
      "day": 364,
      "content": "\u2b50\u2b50 \u2014 NovaMind Assistant has potential, but the support experience is deeply concerning. Filed a critical bug report two weeks ago affecting my financial modeling workflows\u2014complete silence since. For a platform positioning itself as enterprise-grade, this is unacceptable. The tool itself is competent and reasonably priced, but at this tier, reliability isn't just a feature\u2014it's foundational. Paying for a solution only to have bugs languish unaddressed defeats the entire value proposition. Disappointed."
    },
    {
      "post_id": 978,
      "day": 364,
      "content": "Evaluating NovaMind Assistant for our digital transformation roadmap. The platform shows promise for streamlining our workflows\u2014solid compliance foundation and good integration capabilities. However, we've hit a snag with support responsiveness. Our ticket was escalated three times across different teams without clear ownership, creating delays when we needed timely guidance on deployment architecture. For a regional institution managing regulatory requirements, this kind of friction during implementation is concerning. We're committed to working through this with their team, but support continuity needs improvement. Solid product, execution gap on customer success."
